THE PATH-DEPENDENT EXIT LAB
8953 A/B signals, 101 symbols, 333 days, Min30.
2212 of them reach 2R (25%) — those are the only rows where the
two arms can differ, so they are the whole effective sample.

================================================================================================
THE BLIND POLICIES, for reference
================================================================================================
  always 2R                       +0.0101 R per signal
  always 3R                       +0.0248 R per signal   paired +0.0147 ±0.0081  +1.8 SE

  of the 2212 that reached 2R, 1572 went on to 3R (71%) and
  640 gave it back. that ratio is why the blind version is a wash.

  path of the 2R-reachers: median 11 bars to target, median MAE -0.38 R,
  median giveback 0.55 R, 65% never closed back under 1R.

  POWER. the paired difference is zero on every row that misses 2R, so
  its sd over all 8953 signals is 0.769 (sd 1.55 on the 2212 reachers).
  a rule holding half of them moves ~1106 rows; MDE at 2 SE is about 0.0115 R per signal.

  THE TWO-HALVES CHECK ON THE BLIND ROW — the one thing path_exit.py
  did not ask about its own best policy.
                   always 2R   always 3R      diff      SE
  first half         +0.0157     +0.0060   -0.0097    -0.8
  second half        +0.0045     +0.0437   +0.0391    +3.6

